###Setting up a proportion

Corresponding sides of similar triangles are proportional, so we can set up and solve a proportion:

$\dfrac{\blueE{YV}}{YL}=\dfrac{RY}{VY}$

We picked side $\blueE{\overline{YV}}$ because we need to find its length.

We picked side $\overline{YL}$ because it corresponds to side $\blueE{\overline{YV}}$.

Then we picked another pair of corresponding sides whose lengths we already knew (or which we could express in terms of $\blue{YV}$).

$\begin{array}{rcl}
&\triangle VRY
\\
{\text{short} \atop \text{leg}}
&\overbrace{\underbrace{\!\!\!\!\!\left\{ 
\dfrac{\blueE{YV}}{YL}=\dfrac{RY}{VY}
\right\}\!\!\!\!\!}}
&{\text{hypotenuse}}
\\
&\triangle LVY
\end{array}$
